  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing the Ratification of 1960 Education Discrimination Convention in Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to address inequities in Namibia&apos;s education system, which are heightened by factors such as rural isolation, disability, and socio-economic disparities, further exacerbated by the COVID-19 pandemic. The initiative focuses on advocating for the ratification of the 1960 UNESCO Convention against Discrimination in Education to ensure equitable access to quality education for all Namibian children. The project seeks to strengthen legal frameworks, enhance international cooperation, and secure resources to create a more inclusive education system.</narrative>
  </description>
